l eight TS/Go selections, mixed replacement, Message Box, GASP, identity, relay, permissions, storage, transactions, certificates and independent Rust verification. Wallet fixes are in https://github.com/yours-org/yours-wallet/pull/368; the exact e360e67 CI artifact is pinned.\n\nSource9 `ec3a554d433845e9aa8209d9eb20dde48cba6a2a` freezes 471 inputs and all 698 criteria. Go11 fixes map-dependent ancestry serialization while retaining the full Go10 capabilities and byte-exact transaction/proof checks. The two captured native19 graph pairs fail the old serializer and pass 512 insertion-order and round-trip controls with Go11. Native19 remains a failed, immutable sample with original qualification and Rust receipts absent.\n\nCurrent local validation passes 237 core tests, 1,865 synthesis tests with 92 explicit skips, five Python tests, selector/image checks, type checking, catalogs and standards. The full suite passes with two workers and the unchanged 30-second test limit. Go11 artifact inputs remain byte-identical to the tested source8 artifact: full SDK/host/storage/wallet/RPC suites, nine direct replacement/source-outage predicates and 12 artifact mutation controls. Earlier source8 CI retains 1,830 synthesis passes, one 30-second mutation-test timeout and 126 skips; its remaining job was canceled before any native session. All failed evidence and cost remain retained.\n\nThe PR stays draft while bounded order27 runs exact-source PR CI, one allocated retained-evidence reevaluation and the still-unexecuted native20 pair. Readiness requires original native and integrated qualification receipts, both original Rust results, mandatory frozen parent plus 12 child replay, complete independent image reconstruction and final publication CI.\n\nFull BRC100 conformance remains unproven. The signed-satoshi finding, 12 interpretation/fidelity blockers and six upstream Go Messaging matrix findings remain explicit. Full monetary, operator, development-agent and allocated-capacity 